@startuml automatic-restart-replay
title US-10: Automatic Restart Replay - Consumer Resumes from Last Committed Offset

skinparam sequenceArrowThickness 1.5
skinparam participantBorderColor #555555
skinparam participantBackgroundColor #F8F8F8
skinparam noteBorderColor #AAAAAA
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFDE7

queue "Kafka\nposition.normalized" as Kafka
participant "Position\nConsumer" as Consumer
database "Kafka\noffset store\n(__consumer_offsets)" as Offsets

Consumer -> Kafka : consuming events
Consumer -> Offsets : commit offset after each\nsuccessful batch

note over Consumer
  Consumer crashes mid-batch.
  Last committed offset is preserved.
end note

Consumer ->x Consumer : crash

note over Kafka
  Events continue to accumulate.
  Retention window keeps all events
  regardless of consumer state.
end note

Consumer -> Consumer : restart
Consumer -> Offsets : fetch last committed offset
Offsets --> Consumer : resume from offset N

Consumer -> Kafka : consume from offset N\n(replay missed events)
Kafka --> Consumer : all events since last commit

note over Consumer
  Idempotent writes ensure replayed
  events produce no duplicates
  in TimescaleDB, Neo4j, or Redis. (US-11)
end note

Consumer -> Offsets : commit offset as events are processed
Consumer -> Consumer : caught up - processing live events

@enduml
